target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestDisclosure'
expect: converged must owe nothing
why:    a converged run owes NOTHING, and the empty string is the whole signal: the subcommand turns it into a JSON null and Step 14 pushes with no disclosure. Falling through to the head switch makes a converged run render "no disclosure defined for convergence" as an error, which blocks the push on the one state that is finished.
--- old
	case Converged:
		return "", nil
--- new
	case Converged:
		return "Review converged.", nil
